REGEDIT4

; An absolute InprocServer32 path is what makes the driver visible to
; VirtualDJ. It calls GetFileAttributesW() on that value before loading a
; driver, and a bare module name resolves against VirtualDJ's own working
; directory (C:\Program Files\VirtualDJ), where pipeasio64.dll is not -- so a
; bare name makes VirtualDJ skip the driver and report that it needs drivers.
; Real ASIO drivers register an absolute path for the same reason.
;
; pipeasio-register writes the bare name "pipeasio64.dll", so the virtualdj
; launcher imports this file afterwards to replace that value.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Classes\CLSID\{2D3CA9E2-1193-4C5D-B5FD-38798F3DC074}\InprocServer32]
@="C:\\windows\\system32\\pipeasio64.dll"
"ThreadingModel"="Apartment"
